<Layout title="Workplace Accident Lawyer in Barcelona | Spain" description="Legal guidance after a workplace accident in Barcelona and Spain. Preserve the facts, employment documents and medical records and understand what should be reviewed.">
<PageHero eyebrow="Workplace accidents" title="After a workplace accident, preserve the facts before they disappear." description="Keep the accident report, medical documentation, employment information and any communications that explain what happened. The legal analysis depends on the circumstances." primaryLabel="Discuss the accident" primaryHref="/en/contact" secondaryLabel="Employment law" secondaryHref="/en/employment" note="For a time-sensitive case, include the accident date and any current notification or deadline in your first message." />
<section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><span class="eyebrow">First evidence</span><h2>What happened, when, and which documents already exist?</h2></div><div class="prose"><ul><li>Date, time and place of the accident.</li><li>Accident or employer report, where available.</li><li>Medical records and relevant discharge or follow-up documents.</li><li>Employment contract and information about the job being performed.</li><li>Witnesses or written communications that may help establish the facts.</li></ul><p>Do not send unnecessary sensitive medical or identification details in a first enquiry. Start with the essential context.</p></div></div></section>
<CTA title="Want to understand what should be reviewed first?" text="Tell us the accident date, your employment situation and which documents you already have." label="Contact the firm" />
</Layout>
